{"name":"Fairy Dust","hex":"#ffe8f4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy dust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A magical powder that would give the power of flight to whoever it was sprinkled on.","Any apparently magical ingredient or effect; a panacea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy_dust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paris Hilton","blocks":[{"text":"Paris Whitney Hilton is an American socialite, media personality, entertainer, and businesswoman. Born in New York City, she is a great-granddaughter of Hilton Hotels founder Conrad Hilton. She first attracted tabloid attention in the late 1990s for her presence in New York City's social scene, ventured into fashion modeling in 2000, and was proclaimed \"New York's leading It Girl\" in 2001. The reality television series The Simple Life (2003–2007), in which she co-starred with her friend Nicole Richie, and a leaked 2003 sex tape with her then-boyfriend Rick Salomon, later released as 1 Night in Paris (2004), catapulted her to global fame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Paris_Hilton_at_WWD_Style_Awards_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Paris_Hilton_at_WWD_Style_Awards_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris_Hilton"},{"title":"Fairy Dust (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fairy Dust is a 2016 short film co-produced, co-written and starring Swedish singer-songwriter Tove Lo. The film coincides with the first \"chapter\", or first six songs, of Lo's second album, Lady Wood, which was released on October 28, 2016. The film was released on YouTube and Vevo on October 31, 2016."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/FairyDustPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy_Dust_(film)"},{"title":"Tinker Bell","blocks":[{"text":"Tinker Bell is a fictional character from J. M. Barrie's 1904 play Peter Pan and its 1911 novelisation Peter and Wendy. She has appeared in a variety of film and television adaptations of the Peter Pan stories, in particular the 1953 animated Walt Disney picture Peter Pan. She also appears in the official 2006 sequel Peter Pan in Scarlet by Geraldine McCaughrean commissioned by Great Ormond Street Hospital as well as the Peter and the Starcatchers book series by Ridley Pearson and Dave Barry."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/Tinkclose-1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinker_Bell"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg/500px-St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg/1280px-St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg/500px-St_Bartholomews_and_The_Waldorf_Astoria_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Waldorf Asto